# The canonical URL of the deployed site. Used for metadata, Open Graph tags,
# canonical links, and the generated sitemap/robots files.
# In Vercel, set this to your production domain (e.g. https://writing.example.com).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Database (not required for the initial file-based content layer) ---
# The app ships reading posts from /content/posts as MDX. The schema in
# prisma/schema.prisma describes how to move Post/Author/Tag/Comment/
# NewsletterSubscriber data into a hosted Postgres database later
# (Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres, etc). Once you do, set:
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Newsletter provider (optional) ---
# app/api/newsletter/route.ts currently validates and accepts submissions
# without sending them anywhere. Wire up a provider by adding its API key
# here and calling it from that route handler.
NEWSLETTER_API_KEY=
NEWSLETTER_AUDIENCE_ID=

# --- Comments (optional) ---
# Powered by giscus (https://giscus.app), backed by GitHub Discussions —
# free, no backend required. Install the giscus GitHub App on the repo
# you want discussions stored in, then fill these in from giscus.app's
# configuration tool. Leave any of them unset and the comments section
# on post pages renders nothing (no broken embed).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_REPO=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_REPO_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_CATEGORY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GISCUS_CATEGORY_ID=
